WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.388
A division director announces a priority for the year. People

00:00:03.388 --> 00:00:06.776
should get waiver services started sooner after their plan is

00:00:06.776 --> 00:00:10.165
complete. Everyone agrees. And on Monday morning, almost nothing changes.

00:00:10.165 --> 00:00:13.553
That is the usual fate of a vision. It is

00:00:13.553 --> 00:00:16.941
not wrong. It just is not yet something anyone can

00:00:16.941 --> 00:00:17.280
do.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.798
The first step is a goal people can see. Decades

00:00:20.798 --> 00:00:23.966
of research on goal setting point the same way. Specific,

00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:27.134
challenging goals lead to better performance than telling people to

00:00:27.134 --> 00:00:30.302
do their best. 'Do your best' sounds supportive, but it

00:00:30.302 --> 00:00:33.470
has no reference point, so almost any result can count.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.956
A better goal for a review team might be cutting

00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:40.092
the median time from complete plan to decision from 21

00:00:40.092 --> 00:00:41.660
days to 14 by June.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.398
Notice that the goal belongs to the team, not to

00:00:45.398 --> 00:00:48.786
each reviewer. Plan review is shared work. It moves from

00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:52.175
county to state, and from one reviewer to another. A

00:00:52.175 --> 00:00:55.563
meta-analysis of group goals found that team goals improved team

00:00:55.563 --> 00:00:58.951
performance. In the few studies that tested it, individual targets

00:00:58.951 --> 00:01:02.339
focused on personal output hurt work that depends on teamwork.

00:01:02.339 --> 00:01:05.050
A count of plans per reviewer looks fair.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.545
It can also teach people to pick the easy cases

00:01:09.545 --> 00:01:09.960
first.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.797
Now suppose no one knows why plans take 21 days.

00:01:13.797 --> 00:01:17.283
Here the research adds an exception. On new, complex work,

00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:20.770
a hard target can make people anxious and scattered. They

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.256
try many things and learn little. A learning goal works

00:01:24.256 --> 00:01:27.743
better. Within three weeks, find the three most common delays

00:01:27.743 --> 00:01:31.229
and test one fix for each. The June target stays

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:33.670
as direction. The first job is learning.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.157
Every goal needs a limit. Researchers who study the side

00:01:37.157 --> 00:01:40.293
effects of goals warn that targets narrow attention. They can

00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:43.430
also invite shortcuts. In public work, the cost of a

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.566
shortcut often lands on the people with the most complex

00:01:46.566 --> 00:01:49.703
needs. So write the guardrails first. Accuracy must hold. Appeal

00:01:49.703 --> 00:01:52.839
rates must not rise. Complex plans must not wait longer

00:01:52.839 --> 00:01:53.780
than the rest.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.770
Check those lines every time you check progress.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.199
Then make the first step concrete. In a large workplace

00:02:00.199 --> 00:02:03.278
experiment, asking employees to write down the date and time

00:02:03.278 --> 00:02:06.356
they would get a flu shot raised vaccination rates. Writing

00:02:06.356 --> 00:02:09.435
only the date did not have a clear effect. The

00:02:09.435 --> 00:02:12.514
same idea works for a team plan. On Tuesday after

00:02:12.514 --> 00:02:15.593
the team meeting, two program consultants pull ten stalled cases

00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:17.440
and note where each one stopped.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.888
Finally, use the vision to choose. You will have two

00:02:20.888 --> 00:02:23.986
good options and time for one. Ask which one is

00:02:23.986 --> 00:02:27.085
more likely to get services started sooner. Then explain your

00:02:27.085 --> 00:02:30.183
choice in those words. A vision earns its place when

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:33.281
it helps a team say no to something good, for

00:02:33.281 --> 00:02:34.830
a reason everyone can see.
